# Batch files must keep CRLF in the repository itself.
#
# core.autocrlf is on for this machine, which strips the CR when a file is
# committed. The working copy is then fine but the stored blob is LF, so anyone
# who downloads the raw file gets a .bat that CMD mis-splits - it reports a syntax
# error on a line that looks correct. Marking them as non-text stores the exact
# bytes that were tested.
*.bat -text
